[h2]Lite vs. the full version[/h2]
Everything that needed Lua or overriding game files was left out:
[list]
[*][b]No talents[/b]: the full version adds First Responder and Always Prepared to the medic talent tree. In Lite, anyone can fabricate the vest, the Medical Backpack and the Large Medical Bag.
[*][b]No surgical kits[/b]: the Large and Basic Surgical Kits for Neurotrauma / NTCS are only in the full version.
[*][b]No uniform pockets[/b]: in the full version (with LuaCs), the Medkit and the IFAK fit into uniform pockets and open straight from there.
[/list]
Item identifiers are the same, so saves work with both versions, but [b]don't enable both at once[/b].
Full version: [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3841432149]Steam Workshop[/url] · [url=https://github.com/DawidZZ/medkits-assorted]GitHub[/url]

[h2]Feedback[/h2]
If you find any bugs, have any suggestions/feature requests/balance notes, want support for your language (I can translate it with an LLM or use a translation sent by a volunteer), or would like to contribute assets that aren't AI-generated, contact me via Steam or GitHub.

[h2]Details[/h2]
[list]
[*]Game version: 1.13.5.0 or newer.
[*]Languages: English, Polish.
[*]Source code: [url=https://github.com/DawidZZ/medkits-assorted-lite]GitHub[/url], licensed under GPL v3.
[/list]
